        {
          "id": "krea2mood397-74a59c6fe9d04c",
          "alias": "Tessellation-Based Illustration",
          "prompt": "Style: A geometrically disciplined illustration style built on repeating interlocking shapes that fit together with mathematical precision leaving no gap between forms, flat, confidently bounded regions replacing any curved or blended transition, a rhythmic, meditative pattern-logic that treats the repeated unit itself as the compositional subject, confident symmetry and rotational repetition guiding the eye across the entire extent, and a hypnotic, meticulous graphic intensity rooted in centuries of geometric-pattern discipline. Influenced by: M.C. Escher, Islamic geometric-pattern tradition, tessellation-based printmaking technique, mathematical-illustration practice.. Subject:{prompt}",
