        {
          "id": "krea2mood397-15e3761735cb4b",
          "alias": "Plastic Arts Sculpture",
          "prompt": "Style: A synthetic figure built from glossy injection-molded vinyl and matte PVC, seam lines running subtly like a high-end designer art, the surface catching light with sharp specular falloff and glassy resin shine, translucent plastic edges glowing with internal light diffusion, microscopic surface scratches visible across the clear coat, soft gradient cyclorama lighting, soft shadows fall, the entire form reading as a physical collectible object rendered with ray-traced precision and shallow depth of field. Influenced by: Michael Lau's vinyl sculptures, Coarse's minimalism, KAWS' glossy sculpture, Parra's clean graphics, the rotocast vinyl tradition, the soft vinyl kaiju manufacturing aesthetic, and high-end product visualization photography.. Subject:{prompt}",
