        {
          "id": "krea2mood397-cc0c114ab2b748",
          "alias": "Kintsugi-Inspired Digital Art",
          "prompt": "Style: A contemplative repair-as-beauty illustration style built on deliberate fracture lines traced with luminous, precious-metal seams that transform breakage into ornamental focal points, a quiet philosophical tension between damage and restoration rendered with meticulous, reverent craftsmanship, smooth surrounding surfaces contrasted against the raised, textural presence of the mended seams, a hushed, contemplative stillness that treats imperfection as the compositional centerpiece rather than something hidden, and a refined, wabi-sabi sincerity that finds quiet grandeur in visible history. Influenced by: traditional kintsugi ceramic-repair technique, wabi-sabi aesthetic philosophy, Japanese lacquer-craft tradition, contemporary repair-art practice.. Subject:{prompt}",
