        {
          "id": "krea2mood397-fc2e1bce2a2d4e",
          "alias": "Mad Magazine Cover Art",
          "prompt": "Style: satirical caricature composition anchored by a central caricatured subject rendered with exaggerated proportions, grotesque distorted vibes, meticulously crosshatched shading and stippled textures building a grotesque yet highly detailed surface,overly-exaggerated grimacing subject, the linework loose but masterfully controlled with varying pen weights, the atmosphere relentlessly irreverent, mischievous, and subversive, parody. Influenced by: Mort Drucker's cinematic caricature mastery, Jack Davis's frantic crosshatched scene, Don Martin's rubbery distortions, classic EC Comics, propaganda-poster parody of early Mad magazine,. Subject:{prompt}",
