        {
          "id": "krea2mood397-de4cc20af7a443",
          "alias": "Agnes Cecile Style",
          "prompt": "Style: A delicately dissolving watercolor illustration style built on translucent washes that bleed and diffuse outward from a sharply rendered focal point, a deliberate contrast between crisp, precise detail at the center and loose, dripping fluidity toward the edges, ethereal fragmented form that seems to be dissolving into or emerging from pure pigment, a hushed, melancholic tenderness carried through soft tonal gradation, and a poetic, emotionally raw fragility that treats controlled dissolution as the compositional heart of the piece. Influenced by: Agnes Cecile, watercolor-and-ink illustration technique, contemporary fine-art dissolution practice, expressive wet-media portraiture method.. Subject:{prompt}",
