        {
          "id": "krea2mood397-4b043714e5594a",
          "alias": "Graffiti Painting",
          "prompt": "Style: A bold, kinetic street-art illustration style built on dynamic, exaggerated linework with dripping, spray-textured edges that carry raw improvisational energy, confident layered tagging and lettering integrated directly into the composition as rhythmic graphic accents, a rough, unpolished texture that embraces overspray and imperfection as part of its character, aggressive diagonal composition charged with urgent, rebellious momentum, and a raw, unapologetic street-culture intensity that feels loud, immediate, and defiantly handmade. Influenced by: Jean-Michel Basquiat, spray-paint stencil technique, New York subway graffiti tradition, street-art muralism.. Subject:{prompt}",
