        {
          "id": "krea2mood397-770c730c079645",
          "alias": "Ashcan School Style",
          "prompt": "Style: A gritty, unromanticized illustration style built on loose, confident brushwork capturing everyday urban life with raw, unpolished honesty, muted, somber tonal range applied with heavy, atmospheric shadow rather than bright clarity, a candid, unglamorous composition favoring social realism over idealized beauty, meticulous attention to expressive, working-class gesture and posture, and a grounded, socially conscious painterly gravitas rooted in early-20th-century American realist rebellion. Influenced by: George Bellows, John Sloan, Ashcan School painting tradition, early-20th-century American Realist movement.. Subject:{prompt}",
