        {
          "id": "krea2mood397-87b3cce036c04c",
          "alias": "Charles Tunnicliffe Style",
          "prompt": "Style: A meticulously observed natural-history illustration style built on precise, confident linework rendering fine detail with taxonomic accuracy, restrained watercolor-adjacent washes applied with quiet, disciplined restraint, a hushed, patient attention to texture and form achieved through careful, unhurried observation, a naturalist's rigor balanced against genuine painterly warmth, and a timeless, scholarly sincerity rooted in decades of dedicated field-illustration craft. Influenced by: Charles Tunnicliffe, British natural-history illustration tradition, wood-engraving-and-watercolor technique, field-guide illustration practice.. Subject:{prompt}",
