        {
          "id": "krea2mood397-654e9ccc6e444a",
          "alias": "Cloisonnism",
          "prompt": "Style: A boldly graphic painting style built on flat, confidently bounded color fields separated by thick, dark contour lines functioning like the metal partitions of enamelwork, a deliberate flattening of form that rejects naturalistic shading in favor of pure shape-and-outline construction, simplified, decorative silhouette taking precedence over anatomical nuance, a rhythmic, almost stained-glass compositional clarity carried through confident linear division, and a bold, symbolic graphic intensity rooted in late-19th-century painterly rebellion against academic realism. Influenced by: Émile Bernard, Paul Gauguin, cloisonnist painting tradition, enamel-partition decorative technique.. Subject:{prompt}",
          "description": "397 styles｜krea2_397styles-painting_绘画",
          "image": "ray_style_397_0319.jpg",
