        {
          "id": "krea2mood397-7dc9f984fb3b46",
          "alias": "Direct-Flash Photography",
          "prompt": "Style: A raw, unflinching photographic style built on a single harsh, on-axis burst of light that flattens form and eliminates subtlety, stark, high-contrast shadow falling immediately and abruptly behind the subject, an unretouched, unglamorous rendering quality that captures every texture with blunt honesty, a candid, confrontational immediacy carried through the flash's split-second harshness, and a gritty, documentary-style rawness that feels unfiltered, direct, and unmistakably real. Influenced by: Bruce Gilden street-photography tradition, direct on-camera-flash technique, raw documentary-photography practice, unretouched candid-capture method.. Subject:{prompt}",
