        {
          "id": "krea2mood397-4c2bf728ef8641",
          "alias": "High-Angle Shot Photography",
          "prompt": "Style: A dramatically elevated photographic technique built on a steep, downward vantage that foreshortens and compresses the subject from above, an altered sense of scale that renders the subject smaller and more vulnerable within the frame, a wide, encompassing view of surrounding context made possible by the elevated position, deliberate, considered framing that shifts psychological weight through perspective alone, and a distinctive, compositionally assertive intensity that treats camera position itself as the primary storytelling tool. Influenced by: elevated-perspective cinematography tradition, dramatic camera-angle technique, psychological framing practice, classic high-angle photographic method.. Subject:{prompt}",
